{
  "summary": "Restricts wallet transaction rebroadcasting so transactions are only relayed to peers if they were not already present in the local mempool. Adds a broadcast mode in node transaction submission to relay only upon successful mempool addition, and updates wallet rebroadcast functional tests to verify the behavior.",
  "problem": "Periodic wallet rebroadcasts unconditionally relay unconfirmed transactions to peers that have not yet seen an inv for them. When a transaction is already present in mempools across the network, this redundant relay leaks privacy by associating the broadcasting node with ownership of the transaction.",
  "evidence": [
    "Addresses privacy leak identified in #36403 ('Rethinking Transaction Rebroadcasting'): 'While this is broadcast is limited to peers that have not previously been inv'd the transaction, there is still a privacy leak in this double relay of a transaction, especially so for transactions that are still in nodes' mempools.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Diff is omitted from context, but commit messages indicate changes to node transaction broadcast interfaces, wallet resubmission logic, and test harness refactoring.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Restricts wallet transaction rebroadcasting to only relay transactions to peers if they had dropped out of and were successfully re-added to the local mempool. Previously, unconfirmed transactions were unconditionally rebroadcast to new peers even if they remained in the mempool, causing a privacy leak that signaled transaction ownership to peers. Addresses issues raised in issue #36403 regarding transaction rebroadcast privacy leaks.",
